      "message": "I suggest changing this to:\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_BOARD_POWER_HANDLE_STATE\n  /*\n   * Board needs to do something special.\n   * Note: board MUST call power_handle_state() itself if needed\n   */\n  new_state \u003d board_power_handle_state(state);\n#else\n  /* Let the chipset handle the state first */\n  new_state \u003d power_handle_state(state);\n#endif\n\nThen you can define that config for your board, and put your override in, without having anything actually board-specific in this or skylake.c.\n\nThe board-specific function can do both pre- and post-processing of the state around its call to power_handle_state() if needed, or it can simply copy/paste/modify power_handle_state() if its changes are more extensive.",
